nvestor, you are aware that this is higher than your agreed risk rating and are happy to take on this risk with your pension.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"You have confirmed that you are not reliant upon your pension funds and wish for them to have the best growth potential over a 10-year period and feel a balanced approach to this investment would achieve this goal.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"I would describe my investment approach as: Cautious","cells":null},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"Compared to other people, I would describe myself as: More cautious","cells":null},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"If you invested £20,000 and the value fell temporarily, how much of a fall, over a 12 month period, would make you feel anxious or uncomfortable? More than £4,000","cells":null},{"passageId":"P15","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":"Investment: £110,185 then £0 monthly","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"File notes notes - updated.md","category":"C","quote":"Zurich do not have risk level 5 funds, a blend of a 7 and a 2 has been used to create the below 5.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"File notes notes - updated.md","category":"C","quote":"You are happy to proceed with a Risk rating of 6.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P18","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":"The client's agreed risk level is 5. The risk mapping of the new portfolio is 5 which matches the client's agreed risk level.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Missing component","Weak justification"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

