With The People's Pension, you pay an annual management charge made up of 3 elements - an annual charge,
an ongoing management charge of 0.5% (50p for every £100 saved) and a rebate on the management charge. The management charge is reflected in the price of units. The rebate level depends on how much is in your pension pot. When you take money out, we'll work out future rebates on the value of your remaining savings. For more information, visit www.thepeoplespension.co.uk/charge
To find out exactly how much you're charged, please log into your Online Account at
www.thepeoplespension.co.uk/viewaccount and go to 'Manage my pension', followed by 'Charges'.
From May 2018 we changed the way we add tax relief to your pension pot. Your tax relief is shown as separate
transactions to your own contributions, based on the date on which we received it from HM Revenue & Customs.
